# Release seed for the OpenWrt-main / 6.18 port.
#
# ★ DUAL BAND. The vendor rtl8192cd 2.4 GHz driver (source carried forward verbatim
# from the 4.14 port, same redistribution basis) is now ported to 6.18 and verified
# working end to end on hardware -- AP beaconing on ch6, a real client associating,
# taking a DHCP lease and passing 22.6 Mbit/s of iperf3 traffic, with both radios up
# simultaneously and zero OOM. See docs/PORT-MAIN-6.18-STATUS.md §6 for the four
# root causes that had to be fixed to get there (a timer-callback ABI bug class, the
# vm.min_free_kbytes watermark, netifd's handler_load() only ever loading the first
# wireless handler, and the driver requesting a hardcoded IRQ 6 instead of the DT's
# irq 29). Two hazards remain open and are documented there: reading
# /proc/wlan0/{mib_all,sta_info} wedges the box (so dir842-l2flush must stay off),
# and a recurring "tasklet_kill from interrupt" warning.
CONFIG_TARGET_rtl819x=y
CONFIG_TARGET_rtl819x_rtl8197f=y
CONFIG_TARGET_rtl819x_rtl8197f_DEVICE_dlink_dir-842-r1=y
CONFIG_TARGET_ROOTFS_INITRAMFS=y
CONFIG_TARGET_ROOTFS_SQUASHFS=y
CONFIG_KERNEL_PRINTK_TIME=y
# ---- 5 GHz: RTL8822BE on PCIe via rtw88 (backports) + hostapd ----
CONFIG_PACKAGE_kmod-rtl8192cd=y
CONFIG_PACKAGE_kmod-rtw88-8822be=y
CONFIG_PACKAGE_rtl8822be-firmware=y
CONFIG_PACKAGE_wpad-basic-mbedtls=y
CONFIG_PACKAGE_iw=y
# ---- WAN ----
CONFIG_PACKAGE_ppp=y
CONFIG_PACKAGE_ppp-mod-pppoe=y
# ---- bench / diagnostics ----
CONFIG_PACKAGE_iperf3=y
CONFIG_PACKAGE_tcpdump-mini=y
CONFIG_PACKAGE_ethtool=y
CONFIG_PACKAGE_conntrack=y
# ---- web UI ----
CONFIG_PACKAGE_luci=y
CONFIG_PACKAGE_luci-app-upnp=y
